Title: Chana Chaat Recipe (Chickpea Chaat)

Channel: indianhealthyrecipes.com

Linked recipe blog structured data (schema.org Recipe JSON-LD) — prefer this for method text when it has instructions:

{
  "@type": "Recipe",
  "name": "Chana Chaat Recipe (Chickpea Chaat)",
  "author": {
    "@id": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/#/schema/person/2d7d264cdc5dc6602ee06a087cd3fcb0"
  },
  "description": "Chana chaat is a quick snack made with boiled chickpeas, onions, tomatoes, spices and herbs. This spicy, sweet and tangy tasting street food is delicious and protein packed.",
  "datePublished": "2017-12-20T01:00:05+00:00",
  "image": [
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/chana-chaat.jpg",
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/chana-chaat-500x500.jpg",
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/chana-chaat-500x375.jpg",
    "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/04/chana-chaat-480x270.jpg"
  ],
  "video": {
    "name": "Chana Chaat | Chickpea Chaat Recipe",
    "description": "Chana chaat is a popular street snack made with boiled chickpeas, veggies, sweet sour chutney and spices.\nFull recipe on my blog here:",
    "uploadDate": "2022-04-04T13:44:11+00:00",
    "duration": "PT59S",
    "thumbnailUrl": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1ovb2v-dtPs/hqdefault.jpg",
    "embedUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/embed/1ovb2v-dtPs?feature=oembed",
    "contentUrl": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1ovb2v-dtPs",
    "@type": "VideoObject"
  },
  "recipeYield": [
    "2"
  ],
  "prepTime": "PT360M",
  "cookTime": "PT30M",
  "totalTime": "PT390M",
  "recipeIngredient": [
    "½ cup dried chickpeas ((or 1½ to 2 cups cooked or canned chickpeas))",
    "1 onion ((small, chopped finely))",
    "1 tomato ((small, deseeded &amp; chopped finely))",
    "¼ cup cucumber ((chopped, optional))",
    "2 sprigs coriander leaves ((chopped finely))",
    "1 to 2 green chili (chopped)",
    "1 to 2 tablespoon tamarind chutney (or lemon juice (refer notes))",
    "½ teaspoon chaat masala ((adjust to taste))",
    "½ teaspoon roasted cumin powder ((optional))",
    "¼ to ⅓ teaspoon salt ((adjust to taste))",
    "2 tablespoons sev (/ boondi/ farsan/ mixture or corn flakes)",
    "2 tablespoons curd (/ dahi)",
    "1 teaspoon green chutney",
    "1 small potato (diced and boiled or air fried)"
  ],
  "recipeInstructions": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Rinse chickpeas well under running water at least thrice. Soak them in lot of water for at least 6 to 8 hrs or overnight.",
      "name": "Rinse chickpeas well under running water at least thrice. Soak them in lot of water for at least 6 to 8 hrs or overnight.",
      "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-0-0"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Later drain the water and add them to the cooker.",
      "name": "Later drain the water and add them to the cooker.",
      "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-0-1"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Pour water just enough to cover them or about 1 cup. Cover the pressure cooker.",
      "name": "Pour water just enough to cover them or about 1 cup. Cover the pressure cooker.",
      "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-0-2"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "Pressure cook for 3 to 4 whistles on a medium flame or in the instant pot for 16 minutes. You can even cook in a pot with enough water to cover them. Chana should be soft and cooked well but not mushy.",
      "name": "Pressure cook for 3 to 4 whistles on a medium flame or in the instant pot for 16 minutes. You can even cook in a pot with enough water to cover them. Chana should be soft and cooked well but not mushy.",
      "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-0-3"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "text": "When the pressure drops, open the cooker and drain off the water. Add it soups, curries, rasam, sambar or make dough.",
      "name": "When the pressure drops, open the cooker and drain off the water. Add it soups, curries, rasam, sambar or make dough.",
      "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-0-4"
    },
    {
      "@type": "HowToSection",
      "name": "How to make Chana Chaat",
      "itemListElement": [
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Cool the chana completely. Add salt, chaat masala and cumin powder",
          "name": "Cool the chana completely. Add salt, chaat masala and cumin powder",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-1-0"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Add tamarind chutney if using. If you do not have tamarind chutney simply squeeze in some lemon juice or make your own following my notes below.",
          "name": "Add tamarind chutney if using. If you do not have tamarind chutney simply squeeze in some lemon juice or make your own following my notes below.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-1-1"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Add chopped onions, chilies, tomatoes and cucumber.",
          "name": "Add chopped onions, chilies, tomatoes and cucumber.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-1-2"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Toss all of these and taste test. Add more spices or chaat masala if required. Optionally you may add green chutney, potatoes (boiled or fried) or even whisked thick curd.",
          "name": "Toss all of these and taste test. Add more spices or chaat masala if required. Optionally you may add green chutney, potatoes (boiled or fried) or even whisked thick curd.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-1-3"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Transfer to serving bowls. Garnish with some sev or mixture or crushed cornflakes. Sprinkle coriander leaves.",
          "name": "Transfer to serving bowls. Garnish with some sev or mixture or crushed cornflakes. Sprinkle coriander leaves.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-1-4"
        },
        {
          "@type": "HowToStep",
          "text": "Serve chana chaat immediately.",
          "name": "Serve chana chaat immediately.",
          "url": "https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/chana-chaat-recipe/#wprm-recipe-36870-step-1-5"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "aggregateRating": {
    "@type": "AggregateRating",
